course: dictionary
lesson: 6319
title: Blends: motel
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A blend is a new word made by joining parts of two other words. «A blend joins parts of two words: brunch (breakfast + lunch), smog (smoke + fog), motel (motor + hotel) and hangry (hungry + angry), which is now in major dictionaries.» Look for the two halves and you can often work out the meaning.
explain: Motel is a blend of motor and hotel. The word motor reminds you of cars, and a motel is a hotel by a road for people travelling by car. You can usually park right outside your room, which is one of the clues that tells you what a motel is.
explain: Use context to check your idea. If a story says the family stayed at a motel on a long road trip, the clues are road trip and park outside. Together they show the family came by car and stayed somewhere simple by the road.
fact: «Motel» is a noun: one motel, or two or more motels.
fact: A motel is a hotel by a road for people travelling by car.
fact: At a motel you can usually park right outside your room.
fact: «Motel» comes from «motor» + «hotel».
fact: Motels are common in the USA, Canada, Australia and New Zealand, especially on road trips.
exercise: «The family stayed at a motel on their road trip.» Where did they probably sleep? | A tent in a dark forest | A ship out on the sea | *A hotel by a road for people travelling by car
exercise: Which two words are joined to make «motel»? | *motor and hotel | travel and room | car and park | motel and road
exercise: Which word is a blend, made by joining parts of two other words? | sunny | table | *smog | running
test: What does «motel» mean? | A shop that sells motors | *A hotel by a road for people travelling by car | A tall building in a busy city | A place to park your bicycle
test: Ella reads that the family's motel room had parking right outside the door. What does this tell you? | They came on foot and walked a long way to their room | They stayed in a castle with a moat | *They travelled by car and could park right next to their room | They came by boat and tied up at the harbour
exam: Which two words join to make the blend «motel»? | travel and inn | motel and road | car and room | *motor and hotel
